Figure 5 illustrates that Nano-11 facilitates antigen transport to draining lymph nodes and targets immunopotentiating cells. Flow cytometry analysis (A) at days 1 and 2 post-injection shows that ovalbumin (OVA) formulated with Nano-11 leads to a significantly higher Mean Fluorescence Intensity (MFI) of OVA within OVA-containing myeloid cells in the lymph nodes compared to soluble OVA or OVA with aluminum hydroxide (AH) (B). Furthermore, Nano-11 significantly increases the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among the OVA-positive cells in the draining lymph nodes (C), indicating enhanced antigen delivery and specific targeting to these key antigen-presenting cells.